          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Film/Event Prop Cardboard FAQs</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Why use corrugated for film/event sets?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Lightweight, paintable, knife-cuttable, cheap, and recyclable post-wrap. Beats plywood on speed and labour.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Best sheet sizes for set work?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">1200×2400mm matches plywood standard; 1000×1500mm for prop work. BC double-wall for structure, single-wall for facing.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Can it be painted with set paints?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Yes — prime with PVA-water 1:1 first, then acrylic, latex, or spray paint applies normally.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">How much weight can a cardboard wall hold?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Single sheet on frame: 2kg dressing. Two sheets sandwiched on stud frame: actor-leaning rigidity.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">How fast can you supply?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Stock pallet orders next-day from Balakong. Custom cut/print 3-5 days. Same-week pickup possible.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
